// Refined SPHERE at offset 0, FJC_choices 11 (review 27 Oct 2026, #3): a
// triblock pinned next to the axis (P on layers 1;2), restricted theta 30,
// written in both orientations ((A)5(P)3(A)12, then (A)12(P)3(A)5). The two
// kal rows must agree to the solver floor and theta must be 30 exactly.
// Before the fix the stencil's axis test (2*rlow - r > 0 on an accumulated
// float) KEPT the bond channel that ends exactly on the axis at
// FJC_choices 11, 19, 23, 25, 27, 35, 37, 41 (it evaluates to +5.6e-17),
// which breaks detailed balance (folded operator L-asymmetry 4e-4 here):
// both orientations were refused by the mass audit (theta 29.99879 /
// 29.99956) with an underflow message, and before the 26 Oct audit they
// converged silently with orientation gaps of 8e-5 in mu and 3e-4 in F.
// The decision is now taken on the integer target index; LAM changed only
// at offset 0 for those eight FJC values.
// No direct oracle: Namics carries the same test (LGrad1.cpp:80/97/126/143;
// binary 3e9eafd on this input: theta 29.99370 / 29.99762, mu gap 2.7e-4),
// so the engines disagree here by design. The validation is the
// orientation identity + theta closure, plus the clean neighbours: at
// FJC_choices 9 and 13 both engines keep detailed balance, and Namics
// equals PySFBox at FJC 9 (Omega -2.14606977 both); lattice-level anchors
// in tests/refined_curved_stencil.py (S1, and S6 for the FJC 19 twin of
// this input).
lat : NN : geometry : spherical
lat : NN : n_layers : 12
lat : NN : lattice_type : hexagonal
lat : NN : FJC_choices : 11

mon : W : freedom : free
mon : A : freedom : free
mon : A : chi_W : 0.4
mon : P : freedom : pinned
mon : P : pinned_range : 1;2
mon : P : chi_W : 1.0

mol : solvent : freedom : solvent
mol : solvent : composition : (W)1
mol : poly : freedom : restricted
mol : poly : composition : (A)5(P)3(A)12
mol : poly : theta : 30

newton : NN : tolerance : 1e-10

output : kal : append : false
kal : mol : poly : theta
kal : mol : poly : mu
kal : mol : poly : GN
kal : sys : NN : free_energy
kal : sys : NN : grand_potential

output : pro : append : false
pro : mol : poly : phi
start

mol : poly : composition : (A)12(P)3(A)5
start
